title: Configuration open questions
tags: Configuration
kind: question
status: deferred
summary: Installing without a source checkout, a sync racing an editor, and leaving a conflicted merge for your own git tools.

* ''Binary-only install.'' Installing from a pre-built binary or a package, with no checkout to read the defaults from, needs them embedded in `metafolder-sync-config` instead of read from `--source`. The checkout install is the target for now.
* ''Editing during a sync.'' The sync assumes nothing is changing the working tree at the same time (it is an explicit install step). If that needs hardening, a lock file in the configuration directory is the obvious means.
* ''Resolving a conflict yourself.'' A conflict restores `main` and warns. An option could leave the conflicted merge in place, for whoever prefers their own git tools.
